              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                  has “periodic cohomology” in that there exists
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℕ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \in \mathbb{N}
                  such that its
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integral+cohomology"} integral
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+cohomology"} group cohomology
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+groups"} group
                  in degree
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                  is
                  = succeed ":" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cyclic+group"} cyclic
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %munder
                          %mo ∃
                          %mrow
                            %mi k
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi ℕ
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %munder
                          %mo ∃
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi N
                              %mi k
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi ℕ
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %msubsup
                          %mi H
                          %mi grp
                          %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi G
                        %mo ;
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mi ℤ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ≃
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mi ℤ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi n
                            %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\underset{k \in \mathbb{N}}{\exists}
                        \\;
                        \\underset{N_k \in \mathbb{N}}{\exists}
                        \\;\;
                        H^k_{grp}(G;\, \mathbb{Z}) \,\simeq\, \mathbb{Z}/{n_k}
                %p
                  In this case the possible “periods”
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                  form a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroup"} subgroup
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℤ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
                  (
                  %a{:href => "homological+algebra#CartanEilenberg"}> Cartan &amp; Eilenberg 1956, p. 261 (283 of 421)
                  , with
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi H
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi G
                        %mo ;
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mi ℤ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ≔
                        %msub
                          %mi H
                          %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi G
                        %mo ;
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mi ℤ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^{-k}(G;\, \mathbb{Z}) \coloneqq H_k(G;\, \mathbb{Z})
                  by
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "homological+algebra#CartanEilenberg"} p. 232 (254 of 421)
              %li
                %p
                  Every
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroup"} subgroup
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                  is
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cyclic+group"} cyclic
            %p
          (
          %a{:href => "homological+algebra#CartanEilenberg"}> Cartan &amp; Eilenberg 1956, Thm. IV 11.6, p. 262 (284 of 421)
          )
          %p
          #Milnor2PCopndition.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (Milnor’s
                = succeed "-condition)" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mi p
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2 p
              %br/
              If a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+group"} finite group
              has any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+G-space"} continuous
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+action"} free action
              on any
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-sphere"} n-sphere
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  every element of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/order+of+an+element"} order
                  2 is in its
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/center+of+a+group"} center
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                  satisfies the
                  = succeed "-condition" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mn 2
                          %mi p
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2p
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#pqCondition"}
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi p
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            %p
          (
          %a{:href => "#Milnor57"}> Milnor 1957, Cor 1 &amp; p. 627
          )
          %p
          #ZassenHauspqCondition.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (Zassenhaus’s
                = succeed "-condition)" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mi q
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p q
              If a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+group"} finite group
              has an
              %em orthogonal
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+action"} free action
              on some
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-sphere"} n-sphere
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+homomorphism"} group homomorphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G \xrightarrow O(n+1)
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+group"} orthogonal group
              regarded with its canonical action on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+sphere"} unit sphere
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mi n
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ≃
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo +
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^n \,\simeq\, S(\mathbb{R}^{n+1})
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              satisfies all
              = succeed "-conditions" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mi q
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p q
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#pqCondition"}
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo ,
                      %mi q
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p,q
            %p
              Moreover, if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              is
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/solvable+group"} solvable
              = succeed "-conditions" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mi q
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p q
              = succeed "-sphere." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          (
          %a{:href => "#Zassenhaus35"}> Zassenhaus 1935
          ,
          = succeed ")" do
            %a{:href => "#Vincent47"} Vincent 1947
          %p
          #MadsenThomasWallTheorem.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              %strong (Madsen-Thomas-Wall theorem)
              %br/
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+group"} finite group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              has a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-space"} continuous
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+action"} free action
              on some
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-sphere"} n-sphere
              if and only if it satisfies
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  = succeed "-condition" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi p
                            %mn 2
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p^2
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EquivalentVersionsOfPSquareCondition"}
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  = succeed "-condition" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mn 2
                          %mi p
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2 p
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Milnor2PCopndition"}
            %p
              for all
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prime+numbers"} prime numbers
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              (Def.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#pqCondition"}
            %p
              In this case there exists also a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+structure"} smooth structure
              on some
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-sphere"} n-sphere
              (possibly an
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exotic+smooth+structure"} exotic smooth structure
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              has a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+function"} smooth
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+action"} free action
              on it.
            %p
              Specifically, such free smooth actions exist in particular on all
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mrow
                          %mn 2
                          %mi k
                          %mo ⋅
                          %mi e
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi G
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^{2 k \cdot e(G) - 1}
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \in \mathbb{N}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi e
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi ℕ
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e(G) \,\in\, \mathbb{N}_+
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Artin-Lam+induction+exponent"} Artin-Lam induction exponent
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#MadsenThomasWall76"}> Madsen, Thomas and Wall 1976, Thm. 0.5-0.6
            ,
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#MadsenThomasWall83"} 1983, Thm. 5
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Hambleton14"} Hambleton 2014, Thm. 6.1
          %p
            Classification results on groups satisfying these conditions are discussed in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Wall13"} Wall 2013
          %p
          #FiniteSubgroupsOfSUTwoSatisfyTheSmithAndTheMilnorCondition.num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              %strong
                (Finite subgroups of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi SU
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SU(2)
                satisfy the
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi p
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p^2
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2p
                conditions)
              %br/
              Every non-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trivial+group"} trivial
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+subgroup+of+SU%282%29"} finite subgroup of SU(2)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi SU
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi Sp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G \,\subset\, SU(2) \,\simeq\, Sp(1)
              has a free smooth action on
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mrow
                          %mn 4
                          %mi k
                          %mo +
                          %mn 3
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^{4k+3}
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \in \mathbb{N}
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FiniteADEGroupsActFreelyOnFourNPlusThreeSpheres"}
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MadsenThomasWallTheorem"}
              this implies that all subgroups of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              of order
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi p
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p^2
              or
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2 p
              must be cyclic.
            %p
              Indeed, by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ADE-classification"} ADE-classification
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+subgroups+of+SU%282%29"} finite subgroups of SU(2)
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/binary+dihedral+groups"} binary dihedral groups
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %msub
                          %mi D
                          %mrow
                            %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi r
                            %mo +
                            %mn 3
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2 D_{2(r+3)}
                  of order
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mn 2
                            %mn 2
                          %mo ⋅
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi r
                          %mo +
                          %mn 3
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2^2 \cdot (r + 3)
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/binary+tetrahedral+group"} binary tetrahedral group
                  of order
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mn 24
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mo =
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %msup
                            %mn 2
                            %mn 3
                          %mo ⋅
                          %mn 3
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 24 \,=\, 2^3 \cdot 3
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/binary+octahedral+group"} binary octahedral group
                  of order
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mn 48
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mo =
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %msup
                            %mn 2
                            %mn 4
                          %mo ⋅
                          %mn 3
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 48 \,=\, 2^4 \cdot 3
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/binary+icosahedral+group"} binary icosahedral group
                  of order
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mn 120
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mo =
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %msup
                            %mn 2
                            %mn 3
                          %mo ⋅
                          %mn 3
                          %mo ⋅
                          %mn 5
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 120 \,=\, 2^3 \cdot 3 \cdot 5
            %p
              None of these orders is of the form
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi p
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p^2
              or
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2 p
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MadsenThomasWallTheorem"}
            %p
              On the other hand, the plain
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dihedral+groups"} dihedral groups
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi D
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi r
                        %mo +
                        %mn 3
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi SO
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 3
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D_{2(r+3)} \,\subset\, SO(3)
              have order
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi r
                    %mo +
                    %mn 3
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2 \cdot (r + 3)
              and hence
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+subgroups+of+SO%283%29"} finite subgroups of SO(3)
              may violate Milnor’s
              = succeed "-condition" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2 p
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Milnor2PCopndition"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-sphere"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^2
              are not free (as each element must act by a rotation which necessarily fixes an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/antipode"} antipodal
              pair of points).
          %p
            %br/
          %h3#fixed_loci_of_the_circle_group_acting_on_spheres Fixed loci of the circle group acting on spheres
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              Given an continuous
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+group"} circle group
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/4-sphere"} 4-sphere
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fixed+point"} fixed point
              space is of one of two types:
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  either it is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/0-sphere"} 0-sphere
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mn 0
                        %mo ↪
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mn 4
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^0 \hookrightarrow S^4
              %li
                %p
                  or it has the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+homotopy+theory"} rational homotopy type
                  of an even-dimensional sphere.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#FelixOpreaTanre08"}> Félix-Oprea-Tanré 08, Example 7.39
